t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tFact Sheets\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link is-current\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Releases\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tReleases\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/remarks/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Remarks\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tRemarks\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-item\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tclass=\"wp-block-whitehouse-topper-navigation__parent-link\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\thref=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/research/\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\taria-label=\"Research\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tResearch\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t</div>\n\t</nav>\n\t</div>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>President Donald J. Trump returns to North Carolina today with a simple message: North Carolinians are better off with Republican leadership.</strong> Since taking office, the Trump Administration has driven crime down, put money back in workers’ pockets, and unleashed a wave of advanced manufacturing, pharmaceutical, aerospace, and AI investment across the Tar Heel State.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-making-north-carolina-safe-again\"><strong>Making North Carolina Safe Again</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em><strong>The Trump Administration is restoring law and order — and the numbers prove it.</strong></em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Nationwide, 2025 saw the <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/08/president-trump-delivers-largest-drop-in-violent-crime-in-american-history/\">largest annual drop</a> in violent crime on record — a trend that continues to accelerate this year.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In North Carolina, crime <a href=\"https://www.ncdps.gov/division/governors-crime-commission/trends-reported-crime-nc-january-june-2026/download?attachment\">fell</a> across all four major categories in the first half of this year compared with the same period last year, including a 12.4% drop in murders, an 18% drop in robberies, and a 23% drop in motor vehicle thefts. Violent crime and motor vehicle thefts also <a href=\"https://cde.ucr.cjis.gov/LATEST/webapp/#/pages/explorer/crime/crime-trend\">fell</a> in 2025 compared with 2024, including an 18% drop in homicides, a 21% drop in motor vehicle thefts, a 20% drop in robberies, and a 14% drop in aggravated assaults.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In Charlotte, overall crime <a href=\"https://www.charlottenc.gov/cmpd/News-Information/Crime-Statistics-Report\">fell</a> 9% in 2025 and violent crime fell 21%, including a 13% drop in homicides, a 24% drop in robberies, and a 20% drop in aggravated assaults. In the first half of 2026, overall crime fell another 16%, violent crime fell 8%, and property crime fell 17%.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In Raleigh, violent crime and property crime <a href=\"https://cityofraleigh0drupal.blob.core.usgovcloudapi.net/drupal-prod/COR23/rpd-crime-data-26q2.pdf\">dropped</a> in the second quarter of this year compared with last year, including a 33% drop in homicides.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>In Wilmington, overall crime <a href=\"https://www.wect.com/2026/03/26/give-us-praise-give-us-criticism-wilmington-police-report-drop-2025-crime-statistics/\">fell</a> 16% in 2025, with violent crime down 17% and motor vehicle theft down 22%.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>The Trump Administration is swiftly removing the worst of the worst criminal illegal aliens from North Carolina, with <a href=\"https://www.ice.gov/news/releases/operation-charlottes-web-ice-arrests-criminal-illegal-alien-who-killed-15-year-old#:~:text=DHS%20launched%20Operation,1%2C300%20illegal%20aliens\">Operation Charlotte’s Web</a> alone producing more than 1,300 arrests.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-tax-relief-for-north-carolina-workers-families-and-seniors\"><strong>Tax Relief for North Carolina Workers, Families, and Seniors</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em><strong>President Trump’s and Republicans’ historic Working Families Tax Cuts are putting money back where it belongs: in the pockets of the people who earned it.</strong></em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>No Tax on Social Security:</strong> About 1.9 million North Carolina seniors <a href=\"https://www.realtor.com/advice/hyperlocal/north-carolina-retirees-senior-tax-deduction/\">benefit</a> from the new senior deduction.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Bigger Refunds:</strong> This filing season <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/07/one-year-later-president-trumps-working-families-tax-cuts-are-delivering-for-american-workers/\">delivered</a> larger refunds nationwide, with the average refund up more than 11%. In North Carolina, taxpayers saw average refunds of <a href=\"https://upgradedpoints.com/news/average-tax-refunds-by-state-county/\">$3,542</a>.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rural Health Investments:</strong> North Carolina <a href=\"https://www.cms.gov/newsroom/press-releases/cms-announces-50-billion-awards-strengthen-rural-health-all-50-states#:~:text=%C2%A0North%20Carolina-,%24213%2C008%2C356,-North%20Dakota\">secured</a> <a href=\"https://www.carolinajournal.com/nc-receives-213-million-from-cms-for-rural-health-care/#:~:text=%E2%80%9CNorth%20Carolina%20has%20the%20second%2Dlargest%20rural%20population%20in%20America%2C%20home%20to%207.6%25%20of%20our%20nation%E2%80%99s%20rural%20residents%2C%E2%80%9D%20said\">$213 million</a> in first-year Rural Health Transformation Program funding — <a href=\"https://www.ncdhhs.gov/news/press-releases/2025/12/29/north-carolina-awarded-213-million-rural-health-transformation-program-strategic-roadmap-and-federal#:~:text=The%20RHTP%20will,Rural%20Health%20Transformation\">improving care</a> for more than 3 million rural residents and <a href=\"https://www.ncdhhs.gov/news/press-releases/2025/12/29/north-carolina-awarded-213-million-rural-health-transformation-program-strategic-roadmap-and-federal#:~:text=The%20RHTP%20will,Rural%20Health%20Transformation\">supporting</a> more than 400 rural health facilities. The state is <a href=\"https://trumedsystems.com/blog/north-carolinas-rural-health-transformation-program-a-digital-health-fund-worth-watching-closely/#:~:text=The%20North%20Carolina%20Department%20of%20Health%20and%20Human%20Services%20(NCDHHS)%20was%20awarded%20%24213%20million%20for%20Year%201%20of%20the%20federal%20Rural%20Health%20Transformation%20Program%2C%20with%20the%20state%20eligible%20for%20additional%20annual%20funding%20through%202031%2C%20a%20total%20that%20could%20exceed%20%241%20billion%20over%20five%20years\">positioned</a> for nearly $1 billion over the next five years.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protecting Jobs, Wages, and Growth:</strong> The Working Families Tax Cuts <a href=\"https://nam.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/NAM_Tax_Wins_Collection_Final.pdf#page=35\">safeguarded</a> 184,000 North Carolina jobs, $33 billion in state GDP, and $17 billion in workers’ wages.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-an-investment-boom-across-north-carolina\"><strong>An Investment Boom Across North Carolina</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em><strong>The Tar Heel State is winning in advanced manufacturing, pharmaceuticals, aerospace, biotechnology, steel, and the infrastructure of the AI economy.</strong></em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Amazon is <a href=\"https://www.aboutamazon.com/news/aws/aws-investment-north-carolina-ai-cloud-infrastructure\">investing</a> $10 billion to expand cloud computing and AI infrastructure in Richmond County, creating at least 500 high-skilled jobs and supporting thousands more.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>JetZero is <a href=\"https://www.plantservices.com/industry-news/news/55384751/jetzero-to-build-4-billion-airplane-factory-in-north-carolina\">investing</a> $4.7 billion to build a commercial airplane factory in Greensboro, creating about 14,560 jobs — the largest job announcement in state history.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Johnson &amp; Johnson is <a href=\"https://www.jnj.com/media-center/press-releases/johnson-johnson-continues-u-s-investment-with-2-billion-commitment-to-enable-manufacturing-at-state-of-the-art-north-carolina-facility\">investing</a> $2 billion to build a manufacturing campus in Wilson, creating more than 500 high-wage manufacturing jobs and thousands of construction jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Genentech is <a href=\"https://www.gene.com/media/press-releases/15096/2026-01-20/genentech-more-than-doubles-investment-i\">investing</a> $2 billion to expand its biomanufacturing facility in Holly Springs, supporting more than 500 manufacturing jobs and 1,500 construction jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Biogen is <a href=\"https://investors.biogen.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biogen-announces-2-billion-manufacturing-investment-north\">investing</a> $2 billion to expand manufacturing in North Carolina’s Research Triangle.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>AbbVie is <a href=\"https://news.abbvie.com/2026-04-22-AbbVie-Selects-North-Carolina-for-New-1-4-Billion-Manufacturing-Campus\">investing</a> $1.4 billion to build a 185-acre pharmaceutical manufacturing campus in Durham, creating nearly 750 permanent jobs and more than 2,000 construction jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Prysmian is <a href=\"https://edpnc.com/news/prysmian-adding-over-300-new-jobs-in-1b-expansion-of-nc-facility/\">investing</a> $1 billion to expand its cable manufacturing facility in Catawba County, creating 385 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Vaxcyte is <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2014710226818093427\">committing</a> up to $1 billion to expand manufacturing and grow its workforce in the state.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Merck is <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/1899487664841056713\">investing</a> $1 billion to build a new manufacturing facility in North Carolina.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>US Forged Rings is <a href=\"https://www.plantservices.com/industry-news/news/55360746/us-forged-rings-to-build-new-875-million-factory-in-north-carolina\">investing</a> $875 million to build a new production site in Hertford County, creating 625 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Novartis is <a href=\"https://www.ncbiotech.org/news/novartis-plans-771m-investment-rtp-bringing-many-700-new-jobs-biologics-small-molecule\">investing</a> $771 million to expand pharmaceutical manufacturing in North Carolina.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>STERIS is <a href=\"https://www.manufacturingdive.com/news/steris-invest-600m-sanford-north-carolina-manufacturing-hub/827205/\">investing</a> $600 million to build a manufacturing and distribution hub in Sanford, creating 335 jobs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Coinbase is <a href=\"https://www.axios.com/local/charlotte/2025/04/23/coinbase-jobs-crypto-fintech-talent\">opening</a> a new office in Charlotte, creating 130 new jobs.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-center\" id=\"h-results-for-all-north-carolinians\"><strong>Results for All North Carolinians</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><em><strong>President Trump is fighting for North Carolina workers, honoring the state’s military legacy, and delivering where previous Administrations failed.</strong></em></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Protecting North Carolina’s Furniture Industry:</strong> President Trump <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/09/adjusting-imports-of-timber-lumber-and-their-derivative-products-into-the-united-states/\">imposed</a> Section 232 tariffs on imported wood products, including 25% on upholstered wooden furniture, 25% on kitchen cabinets and vanities, and 10% on softwood timber and lumber.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Honoring North Carolina’s Military Legacy:</strong> In 2025, the Trump Administration <a href=\"https://www.war.gov/News/News-Stories/Article/Article/4063467/defense-secretary-renames-fort-liberty-as-fort-bragg-honoring-wwii-soldier/\">restored</a> Fort Bragg — the U.S. Army’s <a href=\"https://www.stripes.com/theaters/us/2025-02-10/fort-bragg-liberty-hegseth-16791540.html\">largest</a> post — to its <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/1932535772785295803?s=20\">original name</a>, honoring Private Roland L. Bragg, who earned a Silver Star and Purple Heart for his courage at the Battle of the Bulge.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Delivering After Hurricane Helene:</strong> After the previous Administration botched the response, the Trump Administration has <a href=\"https://www.fema.gov/press-release/20260914/recovery-progress-continues-nearly-two-years-after-helene\">provided</a> more than $7.5 billion in federal disaster recovery funding to help North Carolina rebuild.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Recognizing the Lumbee Tribe:</strong> President Trump <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2002073623360934077?s=20\">delivered</a> full federal <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/presidential-actions/2025/01/federal-recognition-of-the-lumbee-tribe-of-north-carolina/\">recognition</a> to the great Lumbee Tribe of North Carolina — fulfilling a <a href=\"https://x.com/RapidResponse47/status/2001808338355441893\">promise</a> he made on the campaign trail.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\" />\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>Thanks to President Trump and Republicans in Congress, North Carolina is stronger, safer, and more prosperous.</strong> North Carolinians now face a clear choice: build on the gains Republicans have delivered, or hand Radical Left Democrats the power to reverse them and bring the chaos back.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov/releases/2026/09/safer-stronger-built-in-america-president-trumps-record-in-north-carolina/\">Safer, Stronger, Built in America: President Trump’s Record in North Carolina</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.whitehouse.gov\">The White House</a>.</p>",
